From c9fd0a9b3f5308e3862c70413e52d0114f587368 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marketto <Marketto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:59:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ENGINES: Add Remaster Layer (HD, 16:9, smooth scrolling,
 texts, voices)

Engine independent helper for remastering 8-bit adventure engines:

- AssetPack: remaster/ pack in the game folder: manifest,
  HD backgrounds (localized ones first), 16:9 side extensions, sprite
  index (RSPR), font atlases (RFNT), corrected/translated texts and
  recorded voices
- Compositor: true colour frame at 2x/3x from the engine's 8-bit back
  buffer; HD background where the original pixel is untouched, remastered
  sprite frames through a per-pixel id buffer filled by the engine's own
  blitters, Scale2x/Scale3x elsewhere; palette fades and gray views on HD
  pixels; widescreen viewport with invented sides or bands; sub-pixel
  scrolling; HD text; classic mode (original frame, sharp pixels);
  vertical stretch for games made for non-square pixels (rows resampled
  with an area filter, 16:9 view and mouse mapping following it)
- Layer: one object per game with the hooks for the engine, F8 (or
  remaster_toggle_key) to switch original/remastered while playing,
  aspect correction from Desc::pixelAspect (remaster_aspect), mouse
  remapping and warping, frame pacing between logic ticks, developer dump
  (remaster_dump) of backgrounds, sprite frames and texts
- Keys (frameKey, textKey) compatible with the graphic-adventure-remasterer tools
- Unit tests in test/graphics/remaster.h

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
